course: dictionary
lesson: 12582
title: A small boat called a dinghy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dinghy is a small boat. You can row it with oars, sail it with the wind, or use a small rubber one that you blow up with air. Dinghies are often used to travel from a bigger boat to the shore.
explain: The words around a word give you clues. «We rowed the dinghy from the big boat to the shore.» The big boat and the shore tell you the dinghy is the little boat that carries people between them.
explain: A dinghy can also be a rescue boat in an emergency. Check your meaning by putting "small boat" in the sentence in place of dinghy. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A dinghy is a small open boat.
fact: You can row a dinghy with oars, or sail it using the wind.
fact: A rubber dinghy is blown up with air, and it is often used for fun or in an emergency.
fact: Useful phrases: «row the dinghy», «sailing dinghy», «rubber dinghy», «tow a dinghy».
fact: The plural of dinghy is dinghies.
exercise: «We rowed the dinghy from the big boat to the shore.» What is a dinghy? | A type of rainy weather | *A small boat | A large ship with many cabins | A bag for carrying shoes
exercise: «Sam sailed a small dinghy on the lake.» Where was the dinghy? | In the car | In a shop window | *On the lake | Under the bed
exercise: «The children blew up a rubber dinghy for the pool.» What did the children do to the rubber dinghy? | *Blew it up with air | Sold it to a shop | Hid it under a tree | Painted it red
test: «When the big boat began to sink, the crew launched the dinghy.» Why was the dinghy launched? | To carry cows across the sea | To decorate the big boat | To bake bread for the crew | *To help people get to safety
test: Which phrase means to pull a dinghy along behind another boat? | knit a dinghy | bake a dinghy | *tow a dinghy | row a dinghy
exam: Jayden says a dinghy is a huge ship that carries hundreds of people. Is he right? | *No, a dinghy is a small boat | Yes, a dinghy is a type of cake | Yes, a dinghy is the biggest kind of ship | No, a dinghy is a kind of weather
